---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const playStoreUrl = 'https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.shym.fullbodymetrics';
const appGalleryUrl = 'https://appgallery.huawei.com/app/C117675459';
---

<Layout title="Full Body Metrics | SHYM356.ORG">
	<article class="app-landing">
		<section class="hero">
			<div class="hero-content">
				<p class="eyebrow">Published Health App</p>
				<h1>Full Body Metrics — Complete Body Analysis</h1>
				<p class="lead">From weight and fat to water and bones, the app provides comprehensive body analysis based on internationally recognized formulas, showing what you need to maintain energy and reach your health goals.</p>

				<div class="download-buttons">
					<a class="store-button play" href={playStoreUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
						<span class="store-label">Get it on</span>
						<span class="store-name">Google Play</span>
					</a>
					<a class="store-button gallery" href={appGalleryUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
						<span class="store-label">Explore it on</span>
						<span class="store-name">AppGallery</span>
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="hero-visual">
				<img src="/apps/full-body-metrics-icon.png" alt="Full Body Metrics app icon" width="320" height="320" loading="eager" />
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="article-body">
			<header class="article-head">
				<h2>Complete Scientific Analysis: Understanding Your Body's True Composition</h2>
			</header>

			<p>Have you ever wondered what the numbers on the scale really mean? Often the traditional scale fails to give you the full picture; it does not distinguish between a kilogram of fat and a kilogram of muscle, nor does it tell you how many calories your body needs to stay alive or how much energy you burn during exercise.</p>

			<p>That is why Full Body Metrics was created to be your personal fitness and health advisor. The app does not offer guesses; it relies on internationally recognized mathematical and physiological formulas to turn your basic data—height, weight, age, and body measurements—into precise analyses of body composition, metabolism, and energy requirements.</p>

			<div class="content-block">
				<h3>1. Ideal Body Weight and BMI: The Foundation</h3>
				<p><strong>Body Mass Index (BMI)</strong> is one of the basic assessment tools for determining whether weight is proportional to height. The app calculates this metric using the standard formula, then instantly classifies the result into categories such as underweight, normal weight, overweight, or obesity according to WHO guidelines.</p>
				<p><strong>Ideal Body Weight</strong> is not a fixed number; it depends on height and gender. The app incorporates trusted formulas like Devine's equation to find the healthiest weight range for you, helping you set realistic goals instead of chasing impossible numbers.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="content-block">
				<h3>2. Body Composition: Fat, Muscle, Water, and Bone</h3>
				<p>One of the app's biggest strengths is its internal body analysis, breaking total weight into core components. It uses anthropometric measurements like neck, waist, and hip circumference to power this analysis.</p>

				<h4>A. Body Fat Percentage</h4>
				<p>The app uses the U.S. Navy Method to calculate body fat percentage accurately based on circumferences and height. This gives you an estimate of fat mass and lean body mass.</p>

				<h4>B. Muscle Mass</h4>
				<p>Muscles are the body's primary calorie-burning engine. The app estimates muscle mass from lean body mass and your activity profile, helping you track real muscle gain.</p>

				<h4>C. Body Water Percentage</h4>
				<p>The app uses formulas to estimate your body's total water, helping you avoid dehydration and spot fluid shifts.</p>

				<h4>D. Bone Mass</h4>
				<p>Estimating bone mass provides insight into your skeletal density and overall structural health, an important long-term wellness indicator.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="content-block">
				<h3>3. Fat Distribution and Health Risks</h3>
				<p>It's not just the amount of fat that matters, but where it is stored. The app analyzes waist-to-hip and waist-to-height ratios to assess visceral fat risk and cardiovascular impact.</p>
				<p>For example, if your waist circumference is more than half your height, that's a clear sign that you need to take action.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="content-block">
				<h3>4. Energy Sources and Daily Burn Rates</h3>
				<p>The app calculates your Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR) using scientific methods like Mifflin-St Jeor, then multiplies it by your daily activity factor to get TDEE: Total Daily Energy Expenditure.</p>
				<p>This number tells you how many calories your body needs to maintain weight or adjust it for fat loss or muscle gain.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="content-block">
				<h3>5. Energy Balance: Intake vs. Expenditure</h3>
				<p>Weight control depends on a simple equation: calories in minus calories out during rest and activity.</p>
				<p>The app keeps precise calorie tracking for protein, carbs, and fats, and calculates exercise expenditure with MET values based on activity type and your weight.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="content-block">
				<h3>Why Choose Full Body Metrics?</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>High scientific accuracy based on proven mathematical and medical formulas.</li>
					<li>360-degree view that goes beyond just weight.</li>
					<li>Clear progress tracking when losing fat or building muscle.</li>
					<li>Simple interface that transforms complex analysis into easy-to-understand results.</li>
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class="content-block conclusion">
				<h3>Conclusion</h3>
				<p>Understanding your body numbers is the first step toward reaching your health goals. Don't leave your journey to guesswork; rely on trusted scientific calculations.</p>
				<p>Full Body Metrics represents a qualitative shift in how you manage your body data, combining the rigor of mathematical and physiological formulas, comprehensive body component analysis, and ease of use. It's the essential digital tool for anyone seeking to monitor their physical fitness with awareness, science, and reliability.</p>
			</div>

			<div class="download-cta">
				<h3>Download the app now</h3>
				<div class="download-buttons">
					<a class="store-button play" href={playStoreUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
						<span class="store-label">Get it on</span>
						<span class="store-name">Google Play</span>
					</a>
					<a class="store-button gallery" href={appGalleryUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
						<span class="store-label">Explore it on</span>
						<span class="store-name">AppGallery</span>
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</article>
</Layout>

<style>
	.app-landing {
		max-width: 980px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 32px 0 48px;
	}

	.hero {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(280px, 1fr) minmax(220px, 320px);
		align-items: center;
		gap: 40px;
		padding: 32px;
		margin-bottom: 32px;
		border-radius: 32px;
		background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(232, 247, 236, 0.95), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.98));
		box-shadow: 0 32px 80px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.08);
	}

	[dir='rtl'] .hero {
		grid-template-columns: minmax(220px, 320px) minmax(280px, 1fr);
	}

	.eyebrow {
		margin: 0 0 12px;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.14em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: #16603f;
	}

	.hero h1 {
		margin: 0 0 16px;
		font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.8rem);
		line-height: 1.1;
	}

	.lead {
		margin: 0 0 28px;
		color: #475569;
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.8;
	}

	.hero-visual {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: center;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.hero-visual img {
		width: min(100%, 320px);
		height: auto;
		border-radius: 28px;
		box-shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.12);
	}

	.download-buttons {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 14px;
	}

	[dir='rtl'] .download-buttons {
		flex-direction: row-reverse;
	}

	.store-button {
		display: inline-flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: flex-start;
		min-width: 180px;
		padding: 14px 22px;
		border-radius: 16px;
		text-decoration: none;
		color: white;
		font-weight: 700;
		transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
	}

	.store-button:hover {
		transform: translateY(-2px);
		box-shadow: 0 14px 32px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.18);
	}

	.store-button.play {
		background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a1a, #333);
	}

	.store-button.gallery {
		background: linear-gradient(135deg, #cf0a2c, #e8435a);
	}

	.store-label {
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		font-weight: 500;
		opacity: 0.85;
	}

	.store-name {
		font-size: 1.1rem;
	}

	.article-body {
		padding: 0 8px;
	}

	.article-head h2 {
		margin: 0 0 28px;
		font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.5vw, 2.2rem);
		line-height: 1.25;
		color: #134e39;
	}

	.article-body > p {
		margin: 0 0 20px;
		color: #334155;
		font-size: 1.02rem;
		line-height: 1.85;
	}

	.content-block {
		padding: 28px 32px;
		margin-bottom: 24px;
		border-radius: 28px;
		background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.96);
		box-shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.06);
	}

	.content-block h3 {
		margin: 0 0 18px;
		font-size: 1.45rem;
		color: #134e39;
	}

	.content-block h4 {
		margin: 22px 0 10px;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		color: #16603f;
	}

	.content-block p {
		margin: 0 0 16px;
		color: #334155;
		line-height: 1.85;
	}

	.content-block ul {
		margin: 0;
		padding-left: 22px;
		color: #334155;
	}

	[dir='rtl'] .content-block ul {
		padding-left: 0;
		padding-right: 22px;
	}

	.content-block li {
		margin-bottom: 10px;
		line-height: 1.8;
	}

	.conclusion {
		border: 1px solid rgba(56, 132, 81, 0.15);
		background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(239, 250, 243, 0.9), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.98));
	}

	.download-cta {
		padding: 32px;
		margin-top: 8px;
		text-align: center;
		border-radius: 28px;
		background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.96);
		box-shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.06);
	}

	.download-cta h3 {
		margin: 0 0 22px;
		font-size: 1.6rem;
	}

	.download-cta .download-buttons {
		justify-content: center;
	}

	@media (max-width: 820px) {
		.hero {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			text-align: center;
		}

		[dir='rtl'] .hero {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.download-buttons {
			justify-content: center;
		}

		.store-button {
			align-items: center;
		}

		.content-block {
			padding: 24px 20px;
		}
	}
</style>
